Since April, people have told us their bookings land on the wrong day: a month flipped. The export records 412 distinct reports merged into #4471. Its rows show two different causes.

## Cause breakdown

<IncidentCauseTable ticket={4471} {issueUrls} />

The table deduplicates overlapping export rows by report ID, then counts each report once under its tenant-specific cause. Intake tags are clues, not the source of truth. The one-day-move reports are a symptom, not a separate cause.

## Why these are separate

- **Parser:** the shared parser reads month first. For tenants that write dates day first, this swaps month and day. [Ticket #1](https://github.com/maciaszek/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) covers these reports.
- **Hint:** booking-v3 displays a month-first hint, while the day-first tenant locale controls how the submitted date is read. Customers following the hint can still get a swapped date. [Ticket #2](https://github.com/maciaszek/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) covers these reports.

## Engineering update

The support desk's 5 October update says #4471 is closed. The parser cause is **fixed** by `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`, so its ticket is closed as completed. The booking-v3 hint cause is **won't fix** because that form was retired, so its ticket is closed as not planned.

